 R←Test_Open_092(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;folder;tempDir;parms;success;log;qdmx;threw
⍝ An invalid dependency setting must stop `OpenProject` before Link brings in any code, with a message
⍝ that names the setting. It used to be noticed only when the packages were loaded, after Link.
⍝ *** WARNING: want to rename this fn? Keep in mind to rename its folder under "Tests/" as well:
⍝ ***          the test data is located via this function's own name (∆GetTestPath⊃⎕SI).
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP' ⋄ 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 folder←∆GetTestPath⊃⎕SI
 tempDir←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI
 tempDir ⎕NCOPY⍠1⊢folder,'/*'

 parms←##.Cider.CreateOpenParms ⍬
 parms.folder←tempDir
 parms.batch←1
 parms.ignoreUserExec←1

 threw←0
 :Trap 0
     (success log)←##.Cider.OpenProject parms
 :Else
     threw←1
     qdmx←⎕DMX
 :EndTrap
 →T.GoToTidyUp~threw
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'"dependencies_dev.tatin"'⍷qdmx.EM

⍝ Link was never asked, so there is no code and no open project
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠#.TEMP.⎕NC'Hello'
 →T.GoToTidyUp(⊂'#.TEMP')∊(##.Cider.ListOpenProjects 0)[;1]

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break'#.TEMP'                               ⍝ No check: when all is well it was never linked
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir,'/..'
⍝Done
